, Finnegan started surfing as a child. He has chased waves all over the world, wandering for years through the South Pacific, Australia, Asia, Africa. A bookish boy, and then an excessively adventurous young man, he went on to become a writer and war reporter. Barbarian Days takes us deep into unfamiliar worlds, some of them right under our noses -- off the coasts of New York and San Francisco. It immerses the reader in the edgy camaraderie of close male friendships annealed in challenging waves. Finnegan shares stories of life in a whites-only gang in a tough school in Honolulu even while his closest friend was a native Hawaiian surfer.","nytBestseller":{"provider":"new_york_times","matchedBy":"isbn13","firstPublishedDate":"2015-08-09","latestPublishedDate":"2015-09-13","bestRank":5,"weeksOnList":6,"appearances":6,"lists":[{"listName":"hardcover-nonfiction","displayName":"Hardcover Nonfiction","firstPublishedDate":"2015-08-09","latestPublishedDate":"2015-09-13","bestRank":5,"weeksOnList":6,"appearances":6}]},"readerProfile":{"readerLevel":"popular","narrativeScore":0.279,"accessibilityScore":0.638,"scholarlyScore":0,"traits":[{"id":"memoiristic","score":1,"confidence":"high","evidence":["catalog text contains \"memoir\"","catalog text contains \"personal history\"","memoir/autobiography subject or topic"]},{"id":"popular","score":0.772,"confidence":"high","evidence":["catalog text contains \"bestseller\"","catalog text contains \"new york times bestseller\"","trade publisher signal: Penguin Press / Penguin Random House","major-award recognition"]},{"id":"accessible","score":0.68,"confidence":"medium","evidence":["catalog text contains \"bestseller\"","catalog text contains \"new york times bestseller\"","trade publisher signal: Penguin Press / Penguin Random House"]},{"id":"biographical","score":0.58,"confidence":"medium","evidence":["biography subject or topic","biography award category"]},{"id":"narrative","score":0.38,"confidence":"low","evidence":["catalog text